  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 956 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe subtropical ridge is forecast to become well established\noverhead this weekend, delivering the hottest stretch of the\nperiod. Highs from Saturday through monday are expected to climb\ninto the upper 90s to around 100 or slightly higher in some\nlocations west of the Plateau. Recent NBM and ensemble guidance\nindicate solid probabilities of reaching or exceeding the 100 deg\nmark on the warmest days. Afternoon heat indices of 105 to 110\nwill be common, and warm overnight lows in the mid to upper 70s\nwill limit recovery, maintaining major to extreme heat risk. \n\nRainfall chances remain very low through the weekend and into\nearly next week as dry air and subsidence aloft suppress most\nconvective development. Any activity that forms would be isolated\nand short lived. \n\nToward the middle of next week, global models suggest the ridge\nmay begin to shift or weaken as a northern stream feature \napproaches. This evolution should allow temperatures to moderate \nsomewhat and open the door for increased precipitation chances, \nthough the precise timing beyond Days 5/6 still carries some \nuncertainty.",
